# Profile: lean. An experiment: the smallest ceilings that the measured 1M-event
# peaks (docs/benchmarks.md) leave room for, aiming at a 6 GB Docker VM. The
# scheduler gets 2816m against a measured peak of 2512 MiB, ClickHouse 1536m
# against a sampled 654 MiB (a floor, see the benchmarks doc), the rest are
# their small-profile values. Ceilings sum to about 6.7 GiB and rely on peaks not
# coinciding. Three 1M runs passed on a 7.8 GiB VM (docs/benchmarks.md); it has not
# been run on a VM actually limited to 6 GB. Kafka peaked at 97% of its ceiling.
#
# Applied to .env by `make profile PROFILE=lean`.
MEM_KAFKA=768m
MEM_KAFKA_HEAP="-Xmx384m -Xms384m"
MEM_POSTGRES=192m
MEM_CLICKHOUSE=1536m
MEM_REDIS=32m
MEM_S3=768m
S3_GOMEMLIMIT=512MiB
MEM_AIRFLOW_APISERVER=384m
MEM_AIRFLOW_SCHEDULER=2816m
MEM_AIRFLOW_DAGPROC=256m
MEM_OPS=96m
SPARK_DRIVER_MEMORY=2g
SPARK_SHUFFLE_PARTITIONS=16
GEN_EVENT_COUNT=50000
